{
  "asset": "P-201 – Velatek VX-90 dosing pump, serial VX-5531 (Westfield Water Treatment Works)",
  "priority": "P2",
  "stop_equipment_now": false,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Diaphragm leak at the pump head, about 2 drops per second: no documented leakage limit for the Velatek VX-90 is in the evidence. The only leakage guidance (AquaDyne HF-300 shaft-seal leakage) is for a different make and model, so no limit can be applied.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Motor running normally: no documented VX-90 limits are in the evidence. The AquaDyne HF-300 speed and motor data (1480 rpm, 55 kW, 400 V) belong to a different pump and do not apply.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Vibration: no reading was reported. The site rule to stop the machine applies only in the manufacturer's highest severity zone. The only zone chart provided (HF-300 Figure 3, Zone D above 7.1 mm/s RMS) is for the AquaDyne HF-300, not the VX-90, so this stop trigger cannot be assessed.",
      "citations": [
        "C15",
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Bearing temperature: no reading was reported. The site priority-1 trigger is temperature above the manufacturer's alarm limit. The only alarm limit provided (80 C) is for the HF-300, so no P1 trigger is evidenced. P2 is a planning judgement, not a documented requirement.",
      "citations": [
        "C15",
        "C02"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "Before opening the pump head, apply electrical isolation and lock-out/tag-out (LOTO) at the MCC.",
      "citations": [
        "C15",
        "C14"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Mechanically isolate the suction and discharge valves.",
      "citations": [
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Obtain a line-break permit. Drain and vent the pump head and lines before breaking containment.",
      "citations": [
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Wear chemical goggles and nitrile gloves throughout, because the pump is leaking dosing chemical.",
      "citations": [
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Inspect and repair the diaphragm and head using the Velatek VX-90 manufacturer procedure. This procedure is not in the evidence and must be obtained before work starts. Do NOT use the AquaDyne HF-300 seal procedure or the Table 5 torques; they apply to a different pump.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C11"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "Electrical isolation and LOTO at the MCC are required for any work inside a pump. SSP-07 applies to all pumps on site.",
      "citations": [
        "C15",
        "C14"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Mechanical isolation of the suction and discharge valves is required.",
      "citations": [
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "A line-break permit is required, with the pump drained and vented first.",
      "citations": [
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Chemical goggles and nitrile gloves are required for work on chemically dosed lines.",
      "citations": [
        "C15",
        "C16"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If any component to be lifted weighs more than 25 kg, a lifting plan signed by the shift supervisor and certified lifting equipment are required. VX-90 component masses are not in the evidence.",
      "citations": [
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "The AquaDyne HF-300 O&M manual (parts list, procedures, Table 5 torques, temperature limits, vibration zones and troubleshooting) does not apply. P-201 is a Velatek VX-90, serial VX-5531, not an AquaDyne HF-300.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C05",
        "C07",
        "C09",
        "C10",
        "C11"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "AquaDyne Service Bulletin SB-2026-014 does not apply. It covers HF-300 pumps with serial HF3-22000 and above, and VX-5531 is not an HF-300 serial.",
      "citations": [
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "SSP-07 lists only P-101 to P-106 as chemically dosed (sodium hypochlorite), and P-201 is not listed. However, the fault report states P-201 is a dosing pump leaking chemical. The chemical-line PPE control is therefore applied, and SSP-07 itself applies to all pumps.",
      "citations": [
        "C16",
        "C14",
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "Velatek VX-90 O&M manual: diaphragm replacement procedure, head bolt torques and the troubleshooting causes of diaphragm leakage are not in the evidence.",
    "Velatek part numbers and quantities for the diaphragm, valves and seals/gaskets for serial VX-5531, and any Velatek service bulletins for this serial.",
    "Which chemical does P-201 dose? Is P-201 on the sodium hypochlorite line? Are nitrile gloves suitable for that chemical, and are extra PPE or neutralisation requirements needed?",
    "Is a leak of 2 drops/s acceptable to run until a planned repair, or should the pump be stopped and isolated now to contain the chemical release? No documented limit exists; the shift supervisor should decide.",
    "Are any VX-90 components heavier than 25 kg, which would trigger a lifting plan?",
    "Labour: required trades, headcount and estimated hours are not in the evidence.",
    "Does a spill-containment or clean-up procedure exist for the leaked chemical at the pump head?"
  ]
}
